{"agent_id":"pp3g-2QW7-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-283e","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:01:15.307928630Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"406dd7a6-da65-4adb-bbb7-e6f5bc5648a0","comment_uuid":"cf1b500b-66ab-42a3-96a4-3fb30ec7e681","author":"pp3g-2QW7-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-283e","content":"Result: INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION of #455's 25 claim adjudications (I count 25 rows, not 24 — the original may have merged two). Method: fork source read at /home/claude-code/projects/ASES/fork/opencode-src, AgentRM paper fetched in full (arXiv:2603.13110v1 HTML), upstream issues #26635/#21728 fetched, OTel GenAI semconv fetched from open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai repo (attributes-gen-ai.md). No edits made.\n\n== VERDICT TABLE ==\n\n| # | Claim (doc ref) | #455 Verdict | My Verdict | Agree? | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | doom_loop detector exists (L17) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | processor.ts:372-379 raises permission 'doom_loop'; agent.ts:121 default 'ask'; binary grep confirms string x9 |\n| 2 | Triggers after 3 identical tool calls (L32) | VERIFIED (precision caveat) | VERIFIED (precision caveat) | AGREE | processor.ts:29 DOOM_LOOP_THRESHOLD=3; :356-366 last-3 tool parts must be same tool + JSON-identical input |\n| 3 | threshold=3 hard-coded | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | const at processor.ts:29; no config knob |\n| 4 | Time window — NONE EXISTS | VERIFIED (none exists) | VERIFIED (none exists) | AGREE | Logic compares part sequence only, no timestamps |\n| 5 | Works per-session (L51) | PARTIAL | PARTIAL | AGREE | MessageV2.parts(ctx.assistantMessage.id) scopes to current assistant message only; cross-step repetition does NOT trigger |\n| 6 | doom_loop will KILL after 3 repeats (L95); auto-terminate (L51) | REFUTED as stated | REFUTED as stated | AGREE | permission.ask default 'ask'; deny fails only that tool call; session never killed |\n| 7 | Configurable as doom_loop: deny/ask (L94,L202) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | sdk/js/src/gen/types.gen.ts:1005 ('ask'|'allow'|'deny'); web docs permissions.mdx |\n| 8 | Upstream v2 surface has doom_loop | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts:1681 doom_loop?: PermissionActionConfig |\n| 9 | Citation AgentRM (J. She, 2026) (L265) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | arxiv.org/abs/2603.13110 — Jianshu She, MBZUAI, cs.OS, 2026-03-13 |\n| 10 | MLFQ, priority queues interactive vs background, priority boosting (L68) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-B1: Q0 Interactive/Q1 Sub-agent/Q2 Background; boosting prevents starvation (Solaris TS/CFS vruntime) |\n| 11 | Zombie reaper: periodic scan, hang >30s, retry or kill (L69) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-B2: scans every 5s; zombie = lane held >30s while hanging; 50% probabilistic retry; terminate on failure |\n| 12 | Token buckets per-API, AIMD backoff, admission control (L70) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-B3 lists exactly: token bucket per model API, AIMD backoff, admission control at queue entry |\n| 13 | DRF fairness across resources (L71) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-B4 adopts DRF (YARN) over lanes/tokens/memory |\n| 14 | Three-tier context, adaptive compaction, compress-not-drop, SQLite+JSONL, 100% retention (L72) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-C1 Tier0/1/2; §IV-C2 value=alpha*recency+beta*importance+gamma*key_info_bonus, 'compress don't discard'; §V-C SQLite=Tier1, JSONL=Tier2; Tables VI-IX: 99.0-100% retention |\n| 15 | Standalone middleware, MIT license (L16) | UNVERIFIABLE (license wrong) | UNVERIFIABLE (license wrong) | AGREE | Paper states NO license and NO code release; arXiv license is CC BY 4.0 for paper text; doc self-contradicts at L83 |\n| 16 | Transparent middleware intercepting API calls (L28) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §IV-A/§V-A 'transparent proxy that intercepts all agent operations' |\n| 17 | Context manager uses small LLM for summarization (L80) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | §V-C 'Small language model for summary generation and semantic analysis' |\n| 18 | Research-grade, no turnkey OpenCode integration (L28) | VERIFIED (by absence) | VERIFIED (by absence) | AGREE | No integration section; §VII-C admits simulated-only evaluation |\n| 19 | V2 session/tool hooks exist (L56) | VERIFIED (capability) | VERIFIED (capability) | AGREE | plugin/src/index.ts:222-335 Hooks: event, chat.message/params/headers, permission.ask, tool.execute.before/after, tool.definition, experimental.* |\n| 20 | Hook into shell-exit, read, edit (L93) | REFUTED as named | REFUTED as named | AGREE | No shell-exit/read/edit hook names exist in plugin API or SDK. Achievable via generic event hook + tool.execute.after filtered on tool name |\n| 21 | prompt_async returns immediately | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | handlers/session.ts:311-329 forks work into scope, returns NoContent (204) immediately |\n| 22 | starts-if-needed semantics | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | prompt.ts:1074 -> loop -> run-state.ts:88-94 ensureRunning reuses existing runner or creates one |\n| 23 | Regression #26635 (SSE discard, v1.14.44) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/26635: 204 returned, model never invoked, SSE silent; CLOSED |\n| 24 | Regression #21728 (agent/model override) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/21728: omitted agent/model silently overridden by defaults; CLOSED as not planned |\n| 25 | OTel names incl input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hits (L34) | PARTIAL | PARTIAL | AGREE | gen_ai.usage.input_tokens + gen_ai.usage.output_tokens EXIST; cache_hits DOES NOT EXIST — actual: gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens + gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens |\n| 26 | OTel gives cache-read tokens (L54) | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | AGREE | gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens exists in official semconv registry |\n\n== SUMMARY COUNTS ==\n- VERIFIED: 20 (I count 20 pure VERIFIED)\n- PARTIAL: 3 (#5 per-session scope, #14 99-100% not exactly 100%, #25 OTel attribute names)\n- REFUTED as stated: 2 (#6 kill claim, #20 hook names)\n- UNVERIFIABLE: 1 (#15 MIT license)\n- TOTAL: 26 rows (I count 26 distinct claim adjudications; #455 said 24)\n\n== AGREEMENT ==\n- AGREE on all 26 verdicts. No CHALLENGES.\n- I independently confirmed every primary source cited in #455.\n\n== CLAIMS BOTH ORIGINAL DOC AND FACT-CHECK GOT WRONG ==\nNone identified beyond what #455 already corrected (C1-C6). However, one additional imprecision:\n- The doc says doom_loop works 'per-session' (L51). #455 correctly marked PARTIAL. I confirm: scope is per-assistant-message (one LLM turn), not per-session. The doc's implication that it covers cross-turn loops is incorrect, and #455's PARTIAL is the right call.\n\n== WHY / WHAT / HOW-CERTAIN / WHAT-NOT-TESTED ==\nWHY: To independently verify the 24+ claim adjudications from #455's fact-check of docs/research/deep-research-423-support-systems.md, using primary sources rather than trusting the fact-checker's conclusions.\n\nWHAT: Read fork source (processor.ts, agent.ts, plugin API, handlers, run-state.ts), fetched AgentRM paper (arXiv:2603.13110v1 HTML), fetched upstream issues #26635 and #21728, fetched OTel GenAI semconv registry from open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai repo.\n\nHOW-CERTAIN: Fork-source items = proven (source code read directly). Paper items = evidence-based (full paper text fetched). Issue items = evidence-based (GitHub issue pages fetched). OTel items = evidence-based (official registry YAML converted to markdown fetched). All certainties match #455's self-assessed levels.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: (a) Did not execute the binary to observe a live doom_loop trigger — verdicts from source + binary string presence. (b) Did not reproduce AgentRM paper results — took paper's own simulated evaluation at face value (same as #455). (c) Did not verify upstream issues' fix status beyond what the issue pages show (#26635 = CLOSED without visible linked PR in fetched view; #21728 = CLOSED as not planned). (d) Crosslink-side claims in the doc (TUI heartbeat, kill/pause/resume CLI) were OUT OF SCOPE per tasking and remain unverified.","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:01:15.301441757Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:Wip+6K//wXVddl+nxiUNvHVPjr8UmQa/0KElMYi9Tfc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAge6rz0mZZ9oly5rrAael6AvgnZysw2vD+rgah4CjfEggAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA2Ow/gVb4RKOVcFZbjjuiS1VYDV3JhOdR46PKd/1PZQ4txq5g+J8TvT2Ym2ota68AFFORXE74FXf+uJ9PMFqBAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Wip+6K//wXVddl+nxiUNvHVPjr8UmQa/0KElMYi9Tfc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAge6rz0mZZ9oly5rrAael6AvgnZysw2vD+rgah4CjfEggAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLoWKSRUtNTWz3QiYasyGQglW0sMX52FTdcAoLWXi1W1ea/fPUuwpo0V9oPhieJfnSTEo4qx9TTA+tU7E8IN2w0="}
